Fix the image rendering issue in my web app where images appear cut off or zoomed differently on iPad, tablet, and desktop screens.

Requirements:

1. Images must NEVER appear cropped unintentionally across devices.
2. Maintain a consistent aspect ratio on all screen sizes.
3. Do NOT stretch or distort images.
4. The full image should be visible whenever possible.
5. The layout must remain responsive and unchanged.
6. Do NOT modify surrounding components or page structure.
7. The solution must work in Safari on iPadOS as well as Chrome and desktop browsers.

Implementation rules:

- Wrap images inside a responsive container.
- Use CSS aspect-ratio to control shape.
- Use object-fit: contain to prevent cropping.
- Center the image inside the container.
- Prevent overflow issues.
- Avoid fixed height values.
- Ensure images scale proportionally.

Apply this pattern:

HTML:
<div class="responsive-image">
  <img src="IMAGE_SOURCE" alt="image">
</div>

CSS:
.responsive-image {
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  overflow: hidden;
  display: block;
}

.responsive-image img {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: contain;
  object-position: center;
}

Also ensure images are responsive using:

img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

Do not introduce new visual elements or change image content.
Only fix scaling, cropping, and responsiveness issues.

